oughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.49 vs 5y 0.96), so read it loosely.","About $13.8M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 48% in the 2020 crash and 44% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 30% below its DCF fair value of $75.91, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 28%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $58.05 to $101 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: P/FCF 15.0 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 27% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 6.7% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 5 covering analysts target $75.00 on average, 40% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 9.5% by 13pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.90).","It runs a 18% gross margin and converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.17x.","ROE of 20% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.1% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.4x net debt to EBITDA ($11.3M of cash against $35.6M of debt), with interest covered 15.8x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 4.7, in the safe zone).","The Beneish M-score (-2.15) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.2% over 3 years and 2.6% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 1.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 53%.","Capex runs only 0.2x depreciation (0.6% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 8, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 7.1%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 79%.","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 19 sales over the past year, net $2.5M sold.","The share count has grown 2.6% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 10.7% of the float, 4.2 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,100 employees, each generates about $308K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.6M (5x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":80,"head":"Invest: trades 30% below fair value of $75.91; ROIC 22.4% vs WACC 9.5%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 48, gates 14/26)","Trades 30% below fair value of $75.91","ROIC 22.4% vs WACC 9.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 0.4x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["12-1 month momentum -38%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":64.52,"vc":{"base":75.91,"base_src":"dcf","bear":58.05,"bull":101.46,"alt_median":43.51,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.7446,"dispersion":0.2769,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 74% above the other models' median ($43.51)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"LMB","date":"2026-11-06"}